// guard is asked on three roads (the guard false, true, true).
//   NEWLY ACCEPTED, each refused before this landing because the pick wasn't total to definite assignment: what the arm
//   that always runs ASSIGNS (`n1`, `n4` in a value pick, `n5` consuming, `n9` over a field, `n10` with no bindings),
//   TESTS (`n2`, and `n7` on the error road) or SEALS (`n6`) holds after the pick; so does what a guarded arm and the
//   plain one after it both do (`n3`), and what the plain one does when the guarded one leaves (`n8`). Without the rule
//   this file doesn't compile. `n10`'s `(P1 { })` is taken by the parser today and no reference shows it; DEF-554's fix
//   refuses the form (ruled 2026-11-04, management_21, 21:53 EST), and `n10` leaves this file there.
//   CONTROLS, accepted before and after with the same text emitted: no rewrite (`c1c`, `k1c` over a field, `k2c` over a
//   call's result, `x2k` and `x3k` behind a guarded arm), a rewrite tested again after the pick (`k3c`), an arm
//   assigning what was initialised (`k4c`).
